00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.789 align:start position:0%
the protests have become a weekly event  and follow a now predictable pattern  they begin as a peaceful march the  demonstrators sometimes being closely  shadowed by police then clashes break  out  and next gunfire as the police attempt  to disperse the crowds  some demonstrators appear to be armed  and the bullets do not only fly in one  direction  the protesters insist they will carry on  until their demands are met  we came to say we want fuel and gas  stations we need money transfers and u.s  dollars we want the cost of living in  haiti to come down we want insecurity to  come down  haiti must be paradise for everyone not  for a small group only the people have  their demands  everything we are asking for must be  clear  otherwise we will never stop the protest  today the system must learn because the  haitian people want to change their  country  the prime minister says his government  is aware of the seriousness of the  situation  and has pledged to fight poverty and  ensure that more fuel is available at  gas stations  but for most in the streets these are  empty promises and the message is clear  the protests will continue until the  long postponed election is held and a  new government replaces the old  mike hanna al jazeera
 

